      "description": "tag:jobs.montevallo.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs University Of Montevallo: All Jobs 2026-09-04T11:17:36-05:00 https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10524 2026-09-04T11:17:35-05:00 2026-09-04T11:17:36-05:00 Student Office Assistant, Counseling Services Counseling Services Department https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10310 2026-05-12T12:25:14-05:00 2026-05-12T12:25:15-05:00 Clinical Instructor, Speech-Language Pathology (Full Time) <div>FULL POSITNG<strong><br></strong><br></div><div>The University of Montevallo’s Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology housed within the College of Health Professions invites applications for an Instructor of Speech Language Pathology. The position is a full-time, 9-month faculty position. There is opportunity for advancement to Senior Instructor. Assigned teaching responsibilities include clinical supervision and clinical teaching of Speech-Language Pathology graduate students and may include undergraduate and graduate teaching. Summer teaching and supervision opportunities may be available but are not required. This position is designed for a dynamic educator committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, student mentorship and supervision, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Supervision and teaching methods, practices, and strategies should be in accordance with current evidence and best practice guidelines. The successful candidate will contribute to the development and delivery of curriculum that prepares students for careers in speech language pathology. Experience and willingness to work with both pediatric and adult populations preferred.</div><div><strong><br>ESSENTIAL JOB DUTIES:</strong></div><div>1. Supervise graduate students, unless duties are adjusted to accommodate other responsibilities.</div><div>2. Manage 1-2 diagnostic groups each semester, as assigned.</div><div>3. Conduct preschool screenings with Clinic Director (an average of 2 per semester) as assigned.</div><div>4. Maintain office hours weekly.</div><div>5. Assist the Clinic Director with Clinic Forum (SLP 579, SLP 580) as needed.</div><div>Essential Job Duties are intended to be examples of duties and are not intended to be all inclusive. There will be other duties as assigned. The individual holding this position will serve as a representative of the University and, as such, shall promote a positive impression by demonstrating a collegial and professional customer-service approach at all times.</div><div><strong><br>KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES:</strong></div><div>Ability to supervise the work of others;</div><div>Excellent oral and written communication skills;</div><div>General knowledge of university operations, policies and procedures;</div><div>Strong interpersonal skills;</div><div>Ability to effectively communicate complex ideas orally and written;</div><div><strong><br>EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE:</strong></div><div>The minimum educational requirement for this position is: Master’s degree in SLP</div><div>Education substituted for experience? No</div><div>This position requires: 3 years clinical and/or supervisory experience.</div><div>Experience substituted for education? No</div><div><strong><br>LICENSES, CERTIFICATIONS, OR REGISTRATIONS:</strong></div><div>Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications <strong>required </strong>for this position include:</div><div>· Current ASHA Certification, must be maintained</div><div>· Alabama State License or be eligible to obtain Alabama State Licensure prior to beginning employment, must be maintained</div><div>· Must possess or complete required supervisor-related training for speech language pathology</div><div><br>Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications <strong>preferred </strong>for this position include:</div><ul><li>None</li></ul><div><br></div> Speech Pathology https://jobs.montevallo.edu/pools/10496 2026-08-21T14:26:04-05:00 2026-08-21T14:26:04-05:00 Vitae Bank 2026-2027 College of Education and Human Development <div>Teach courses as assigned by the Department Chair.<br><br>Temporary faculty in the following areas: counseling; dietetics; education; education administration; family relations; hospitality and tourism; intern supervision in education; human development; instructional technology; exercise science; consumer sciences; hospitality and tourism; Library; and several other disciplines.<br><br>Adjunct Instructor for the College of Education and Human Development serves as an official representative of the University, promoting a positive first-impression by adopting and demonstrating a collegial, customer-service approach to students, parents, faculty, staff and other members of the University community.</div> Pool https://jobs.montevallo.edu/pools/7975 2023-05-24T11:16:50-05:00 2023-05-24T11:16:50-05:00 Vita Bank Library 2023 - 2024 <div>Provide information literacy instruction and research assistance, with a focus on English Composition classes (ENG 101 and ENG 102) for 24 hours per week, including some weekend and evening hours. Participate in staffing the research help desk and chat reference service. Develop and maintain research guides, tutorials, and other instructional materials. Assist with assessment of library instruction and the user experience.&nbsp;</div> Pool https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10455 2026-08-09T20:54:02-05:00 2026-08-09T20:54:03-05:00 Graduate Assistant - Archives Graduate Research Assistant Carmichael Library https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10064 2025-08-13T16:26:15-05:00 2025-08-13T16:26:15-05:00 Student Mail Clerk Central Receiving and Mail Services https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/9866 2025-05-09T10:02:55-05:00 2025-05-09T10:02:55-05:00 2025-2026 Peer Academic Coaches Falcon Success Center https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10327 2026-05-20T22:04:36-05:00 2026-05-20T22:04:36-05:00 Director, Alabama Traffic Safety Center Alabama Traffic Safety Center https://jobs.montevallo.edu/pools/9677 2024-10-21T12:48:30-05:00 2024-10-21T12:48:30-05:00 Vitae Bank 2024 - 2025 College of Arts and Sciences <div>Teach courses as assigned by the Department Chair.<br><br></div><div>Temporary faculty in the following areas: biology; chemistry; communication science and disorders; English; environmental studies; world languages (French &amp; Spanish); geography; geology; history; mathematics; physics, philosophy; political science; psychology; religion; social work; sociology; computer science; and several other disciplines.<br><br>The Adjunct Instructor for the College of Arts and Sciences serves as an official representative of the University, promoting a positive first-impression by adopting and demonstrating a collegial, customer-service approach to students, parents, faculty, staff and other members of the University community.</div> Pool https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10471 2026-08-13T09:09:54-05:00 2026-08-13T09:09:55-05:00 Graduate Assistant - CEHD Graduate Studies College Education Dean's Office https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10071 2025-08-19T21:57:43-05:00 2025-08-19T21:57:44-05:00 Student Technical Support Staff College of Fine Arts Dean's Office https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/9940 2025-06-20T16:46:07-05:00 2025-06-20T16:46:07-05:00 2025-2026 FSC Peer Tutor Falcon Success Center https://jobs.montevallo.edu/pools/4903 2019-11-24T16:39:46-06:00 2019-11-24T16:39:47-06:00 Vitae Bank 2020-2021 College of Education and Human Development Teach courses as assigned by the Department Chair.\r\n\r\nTemporary faculty in the following areas: counseling; dietetics; education; education administration; family relations; intern supervision in education; human development; instructional technology; exercise science; consumer sciences; Library; and several other disciplines.\r\n\r\nAdjunct Instructor for the College of Education and Human Development serves as an official representative of the University, promoting a positive first-impr