parents, faculty, staff and other members of the University community.</div> Pool https://jobs.montevallo.edu/pools/10492 2026-08-21T14:17:42-05:00 2026-08-21T14:17:42-05:00 Vitae Bank 2026-2027 Michael E Stephens College of Business <div>Teach courses as assigned by the Department Chair.<br><br>Temporary faculty in the following areas: accounting; data analytics; Computer Science; economics; finance; information systems; management; marketing; and several other disciplines.<br><br>The Adjunct Instructor for the Michael E. Stephens College of Business serves as an official representative of the University, promoting a positive first-impression by adopting and demonstrating a collegial, customer-service approach to students, parents, faculty, staff and other members of the University community.</div> Pool https://jobs.montevallo.edu/pools/10490 2026-08-21T14:11:54-05:00 2026-08-21T14:11:54-05:00 Vitae Bank 2026 - 2027 College of Fine Arts <div>Teach courses as assigned by the Department Chair.<br><br>Temporary faculty in the following areas: art; communication studies; digital film making; mass communication; music; production operations; theatre and several other disciplines.<br><br>The Adjunct Instructor for the College of Fine Arts serves as an official representative of the University, promoting a positive first-impression by adopting and demonstrating a collegial, customer-service approach to students, parents, faculty, staff and other members of the University community.&nbsp;</div> Pool https://jobs.montevallo.edu/pools/10488 2026-08-21T14:07:58-05:00 2026-08-21T14:07:58-05:00 Vitae Bank 2026-2027 College of Health Professions <div>Teach courses as assigned by the Department Chair.<br><br>Temporary faculty in the following areas: dietetics; nursing; and exercise science.<br><br>Adjunct Instructor for the College of Health Professions serves as an official representative of the University, promoting a positive first-impression by adopting and demonstrating a collegial, customer-service approach to students, parents, faculty, staff and other members of the University community.</div> Pool https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10485 2026-08-19T15:40:17-05:00 2026-08-19T15:40:18-05:00 Assistant or Associate Professor (Tenure-track) Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology <div>The Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology at the University of Montevallo is seeking a candidate for a nine-month, tenure track position in Speech-Language Pathology at the level of Assistant or Associate Professor.</div> Speech Pathology https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10388 2026-06-25T10:42:45-05:00 2026-06-25T10:42:47-05:00 Assistant Professor of Strategic Management (Tenure Track) <div>FULL ADVERTISEMENT:<br><strong>Assistant Professor of Strategic Management (Tenure Track)</strong></div><div>The University of Montevallo (UM) invites nominations and applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Strategic Management, with a start date of August 2027. Candidates with a Ph.D. or DBA in Strategic Management from AACSB-accredited or similarly accredited institutions are preferred; however, doctoral candidates with ABD status will also be considered.</div><div>Ideal candidates will demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and research, along with enthusiasm for mentoring students from diverse backgrounds and with varying levels of academic preparation and career goals.</div><div><strong>About the University of Montevallo</strong></div><div><strong>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;UM is Alabama’s designated public liberal arts university, offering bachelor’s, master’s, and specialist-level programs with a focus on high-quality, innovative teaching and a student body of over 3,000.</strong></div><div><strong>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;The Stephens College of Business is AACSB-accredited and supports both undergraduate and MBA-level programs. The average class size is about 21 students, highlighting our emphasis on individualized learning.</strong></div><div><strong>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;UM recently launched its first doctoral program in Educational Leadership (Ed.D.), expanding its graduate-level offerings beyond master’s and specialist degrees.</strong></div><div>Nominations and inquiries should be directed to Search Committee Chair Dr. Milad Jasemi at <a href=\"mailto:mjasemiz@montevallo.edu\"><strong>mjasemiz@montevallo.edu</strong></a>. Applicants should apply online at <a href=\"https://jobs.montevallo.edu\"><strong>https://jobs.montevallo.edu</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.</div> MESCO Business Dean's Office https://jobs.montevallo.edu/postings/10310 2026-05-12T12:25:14-05:00 2026-05-12T12:25:15-05:00 Clinical Instructor, Speech-Language Pathology (Full Time) <div>FULL POSITNG<strong><br></strong><br></div><div>The University of Montevallo’s Department of Social Work and Speech Pathology housed within the College of Health Professions invites applications for an Instructor of Speech Language Pathology. The position is a full-time, 9-month faculty position. There is opportunity for advancement to Senior Instructor. Assigned teaching responsibilities include clinical supervision and clinical teaching of Speech-Language Pathology graduate students and may include undergraduate and graduate teaching. Summer teaching and supervision opportunities may be available but are not required. This position is designed for a dynamic educator committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, student mentorship and supervision, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Supervision and teaching methods, practices, and strategies should be in accordance with current evidence and best practice guidelines. The successful candidate will contribute to the development and delivery of curriculum that prepares students for careers in speech language pathology. Experience and willingness to work with both pediatric and adult populations preferred.</div><div><strong><br>ESSENTIAL JOB DUTIES:</strong></div><div>1. Supervise graduate students, unless duties are adjusted to accommodate other responsibilities.</div><div>2. Manage 1-2 diagnostic groups each semester, as assigned.</div><div>3. Conduct preschool screenings with Clinic Director (an average of 2 per semester) as assigned.</div><div>4. Maintain office hours weekly.</div><div>5. Assist the Clinic Director with Clinic Forum (SLP 579, SLP 580) as needed.</div><div>Essential Job Duties are intended to be examples of duties and are not intended to be all inclusive. There will be other duties as assigned. The individual holding this position will serve as a representative of the University and, as such, shall promote a positive impression by demonstrating a collegial and professional customer-service approach at all times.</div><div><strong><br>KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES:</strong></div><div>Ability to supervise the work of others;</div><div>Excellent oral and written communication skills;</div><div>General knowledge of university operations, policies and procedures;</div><div>Strong interpersonal skills;</div><div>Ability to effectively communicate complex ideas orally and written;</div><div><strong><br>EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE:</strong></div><div>The minimum educational requirement for this position is: Master’s degree in SLP</div><div>Education substituted for experience? No</div><div>This position requires: 3 years clinical and/or supervisory experience.</div><div>Experience substituted for education? No</div><div><strong><br>LICENSES, CERTIFICATIONS, OR REGISTRATIONS:</strong></div><div>Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications <strong>required </strong>for this position include:</div><div>· Current ASHA Certification, must be maintained</div><div>· Alabama State License or be eligible to obtain Alabama State Licensure prior to beginning employment, must be maintained</div><div>· Must possess or complete required supervisor-related training for speech language pathology</div><div><br>Certifications, licenses, professional designations, or other qualifications <strong>preferred </strong>for this position include:</div><ul><li>None</li></ul><div><br></div> Speech Pathology"
    },
